nodecode-hwiki is a rewrite of ottosulin's ottosulin/hwiki:

  https://github.com/ottosulin/hwiki
  commit d1961956eaafbd64fef71cb7135d475efcc8f954
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Otto Sulin (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's memory provider, whole. The four tools keep
their names, descriptions and parameters (wiki_memory_search, wiki_memory_read,
wiki_memory_write, wiki_memory_status); the store keeps its rules (the curated
wiki is read-only to the agent, writes are append-only dated bullets confined
to memory_dir, a secret-shaped write is refused, untrusted_dirs are never
indexed, recalled or read, a page resolves by path, slug, wikilink or title
and is truncated at max_chars); the ranker keeps its shape (heading-scoped
chunks, prefix-matched query terms with the same stopwords, BM25, at most
max_hits_per_page headings per page, demote_paths filled last, untrusted hits
re-filtered); and the recall before each model request keeps its form (the
"## Wiki Memory (recalled)" block, min_query_chars, prefetch_limit, and a
prefetch_max_chars budget over the snippets).

What was left out, and why: the SQLite FTS5 index, replaced by an index this
cell builds in memory over the same chunks, because a cell bundles no Python
or database -- it is rebuilt on the first search after reindex_seconds, and
after every write; the qmd backend (a Node CLI with GGUF models) and its
reciprocal-rank fusion; the include/exclude globs (every *.md outside the
hidden and untrusted directories is indexed); the HERMES_HOME config file and
environment overrides (the cell's section is the config); the `hermes hwiki`
subcommands (status, search, index, lint, config, migrate) beyond what /hwiki
answers; the optional mirror of the harness's built-in memory writes, because
Nodecode's built-in memory is not this cell's to intercept; and the
`updated:` frontmatter bump on append.

LICENSE is hwiki's repository LICENSE, unchanged.
